# Generated metadata
Metadata/

# Flowthru triage layers: the generated data artifacts are not committed. Only the pipeline's
# code (catalog/schema .cs), curated raw inputs, and the vendored type ontology are kept.
# (Hand-authored NUnit golds live under Fixtures/, NOT here — see below.)
Data/**

# Un-ignore layer directories and their Schemas subdirectories so git can traverse them
!Data/*/
!Data/*/Schemas/
!Data/_01_Raw/Datasets/

# Curated raw inputs that ARE committed: hand-curated card inputs, plus the vendored
# type-ontology.json seeded from the upstream mtg-rules project (nx run mast:seed-ontology).
!Data/_01_Raw/Datasets/Curated/**/*

# Allow all schema and catalog .cs files
!Data/**/*.cs

# Un-ignore all .gitkeep files anywhere
!**/.gitkeep

# NOTE: committed NUnit fixtures (HandParsedCards, KeywordExpansions, MalformedParsedCards,
# FilterRelations, Query, Interactions) live under Fixtures/ — a top-level dir that is NOT ignored,
# so it needs no allowlist here. That separation is the whole point: Data/ = triage, Fixtures/ = golds.
